{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardTableauSpectral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardTableauSpectral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyReduction","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.GetD"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.zero_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.zero_content","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L139-L144","doc":"**The spectral rule's base case is consistent.**  Entry `0` has content `0`, so the rule\n`eigenvalue of L₁ = q^{2·content}` gives `q⁰ = 1` — matching `jmRaw_zero : L₁ = 1` exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.zero_at_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.zero_at_corner","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L112-L137","doc":"**Entry `0` sits at the corner `(0,0)`** — hence its content is `0`, and the JM base case\n`L₁ = 1 = q^{2·0}` is *forced* by standardness rather than chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.zero_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.zero_row","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L89-L110","doc":"**Entry `0` sits in the first row.**  If it were in row `r > 0`, the cell directly above it\nwould also be a cell (`mem_cells_pred_row`), its entry would share the column and sit in a strictly\nsmaller row, and `col_incr` would make that entry `< 0` — impossible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.sum_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.sum_content","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The weaker bijection results still apply: the content of a standard tableau's entries sums to\n`c(λ)`, by `sum_content_of_equiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.col_incr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.col_incr","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Entries increase down a column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.row_incr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.row_incr","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Entries increase along a row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.toEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.toEquiv","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The underlying entries-to-cells bijection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L64-L77","doc":"**A standard Young tableau** of shape `λ` with `n` entries: a bijection from entries to cells\nwhose inverse is increasing along rows and down columns.\n\nThe conditions are stated in the direction that is convenient to *use*: if two entries share a row\n(resp. column) and the first is further right (resp. down), then it is the larger entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.mem_cells_pred_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.mem_cells_pred_row","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauSpectral.lean#L48-L60","doc":"**A Young diagram is closed upward within a column.**  If `(r, c)` is a cell and `r > 0`, then\n`(r−1, c)` is a cell too — because the partition's rows are weakly decreasing, so row `r−1` is at\nleast as long as row `r`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}